Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.23,0:00:16.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong? \NSuddenly, you're not moving so well.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.46,0:00:22.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looks like an artificially created soul isn't quite perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.16,0:00:25.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this what happens when you find out what you really are?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.47,0:00:31.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No... I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.44,0:00:32.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.03,0:00:34.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alphonse Elric!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.28,0:00:44.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you, there's no \Nproof of that. Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.57,0:00:47.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Accept it. You'll feel better.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.35,0:00:48.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that's so,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.94,0:00:50.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what about you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.27,0:00:56.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have memories of when \Nyou were alive. Which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.96,0:01:07.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm so pleased.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.76,0:01:10.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The fools keep coming \None after another today.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.97,0:01:13.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You asked about me?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.59,0:01:15.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.48,0:01:18.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I love cutting up live people,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.62,0:01:22.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and I like killing people \Nso much, I can't stand it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.10,0:01:25.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I kill; therefore, I am!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.16,0:01:30.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am who I am!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.96,0:01:33.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's all the evidence I need!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.20,0:01:42.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need for you to prove your existence.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.95,0:01:47.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.68,0:01:52.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.97,0:01:57.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.70,0:02:03.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.55,0:03:43.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.86,0:03:47.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An acquaintance of yours?! That's dirty! Who knew you still had friends around?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.95,0:03:49.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Friends?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.75,0:03:51.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What, then?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.85,0:03:59.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What the?! What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.99,0:04:02.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have a wretched body as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.43,0:04:06.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,May you find peace with God...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.31,0:04:07.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.32,0:04:11.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is that doing there?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.09,0:04:13.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.78,0:04:15.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.57,0:04:19.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By any chance, \Ndo you not know what that is?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.75,0:04:21.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.27,0:04:24.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you saying this is?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.38,0:04:29.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see, you want to \Nfind out that badly.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.62,0:04:32.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's see now...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.16,0:04:39.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I'm not saying.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.00,0:05:21.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been 130 years, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.94,0:05:38.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is where they keep the animals for experimentation, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.97,0:05:42.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come with me, \Nor go play in hell, you choose.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.70,0:05:47.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Decide now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.49,0:06:06.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These devices are set \Nso I can bust things up
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.32,0:06:08.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and make myself \Nall gone at any time!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.03,0:06:12.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then, it's about time \NI went bye-bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.21,0:06:13.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.19,0:06:20.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you want to find out about your arm, you have to come all the way inside here!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.40,0:06:24.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He got away.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.80,0:06:25.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.40,0:06:28.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.98,0:06:33.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.44,0:06:37.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're here, \Nthen Fullmetal must be inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.65,0:06:39.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,W-Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.46,0:06:41.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait up, I say!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.40,0:06:51.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What was that tremor \Na moment ago?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.77,0:06:53.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good question.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.04,0:06:59.19,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,However, there are explosives set throughout this building, for destroying evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.59,0:07:03.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With that shock just now, \Nthere's no telling when they will go off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.39,0:07:06.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And I still don't know anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.52,0:07:09.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will keep my promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.33,0:07:13.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You came here in search of the secrets of the Philosopher's Stone, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.82,0:07:18.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though I know everything, but I will lead you to the entrance.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.19,0:07:25.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But what do we do \Nwith your brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.87,0:07:28.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't just leave him here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.17,0:07:30.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't need to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.35,0:07:32.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Finish me off, immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.70,0:07:36.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you, \NI'm not killing anyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.31,0:07:42.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said we were people, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.61,0:07:44.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, tell me,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.25,0:07:47.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,how am I supposed to \Ngo on living in this body?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.61,0:07:50.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.13,0:07:53.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't attach him! Don't attach him!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.74,0:07:55.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you implying I should join with my brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.41,0:07:58.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and together, continue guarding this deserted house?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.60,0:08:01.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In this unaging, hollow body?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.76,0:08:03.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You could give this up, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.67,0:08:06.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And what, go outside?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.08,0:08:09.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would guys like us have the freedom to just wander around on our own outside?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.93,0:08:15.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hang on. My own brother has the same kind of body as you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.00,0:08:17.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You see, it's in order to \Nreturn him back to normal
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.78,0:08:19.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that I'm searching for \Nthe Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.24,0:08:22.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I ever find it...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.04,0:08:27.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we were ever returned to being human, we would just be executed again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.33,0:08:30.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.81,0:08:33.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if we became human, \Nwe would just get killed again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.81,0:08:38.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or are you saying that you would turn \Na blind eye to us, a couple of serial killers?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.55,0:08:39.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But still!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.85,0:08:42.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would you treat us as humans?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.38,0:08:44.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sounds admirable in word,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.60,0:08:47.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but if you were to treat us \Nas though we were humans,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.61,0:08:51.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when we can only go on \Nliving in this form,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.20,0:08:53.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do you realize how cruel that would be to us?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.90,0:08:59.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You idiot! What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.65,0:09:02.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just shut up and watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.68,0:09:06.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you saying?! \NHe's your younger brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.78,0:09:10.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm glad that you \Nregard him as a person.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.88,0:09:14.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why he can no longer \Ngo back to being Number 48.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.04,0:09:16.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the only thing \Nhe can do as a person.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.39,0:09:18.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That isn't true!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.93,0:09:22.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, I'm going on ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.83,0:09:26.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.77,0:09:41.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My brother, once I fulfill my promise, \NI will come at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.00,0:09:44.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What were you thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.31,0:09:48.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What were you guys thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.99,0:09:51.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was the only choice \Nhe could make.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.11,0:09:57.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I treated you guys as people, all you could do is die.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.90,0:10:01.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, what was \NI supposed to do for him?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.75,0:10:05.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are many problems in this world for which there is no way to answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.02,0:10:14.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to return \NAl back to normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.78,0:10:16.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not about to allow Al to go through this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.21,0:10:19.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.30,0:10:35.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're really going to \Nlet these guys out?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.03,0:10:38.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was the order. I hear they're \Ngoing to be used in military research.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.46,0:10:41.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even though they have life sentences,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.49,0:10:44.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it wouldn't be surprising \Nif they were really executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.16,0:10:47.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that an earthquake?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.45,0:10:51.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is the sound of the building collapsing due to explosives.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.60,0:10:54.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, what a pleasant sound...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.24,0:10:58.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.20,0:11:03.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, that brings back memories of \Nthe extermination assault on Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.46,0:11:06.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on out! \NYou've been summoned!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.08,0:11:09.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You blew away both \Nfriend and foe there,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.91,0:11:12.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you miserable mad bomber, Kimbly...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.79,0:11:19.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Such a pleasant sound. \NIt reverberates in the pit of my stomach.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.64,0:11:23.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is how far the former \NCrimson Alchemist has fallen.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.74,0:11:32.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now all we need is for Envy to gather the ingredients.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.08,0:11:35.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long have we been \Nwaiting for this, I wonder...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.36,0:11:37.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.46,0:11:40.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.98,0:11:43.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's him! It's him!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.35,0:11:44.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Him{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.16,0:11:46.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.46,0:11:47.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Greed?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.38,0:11:51.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looks like we'll have to hurry,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.80,0:11:54.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,before there are any \Nunwanted intrusions.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.96,0:12:00.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There aren't any more \Nweird traps, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.25,0:12:03.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There haven't been any intruders who have gotten in this far.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.70,0:12:07.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean, because they were all dealt with by you guys?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.62,0:12:12.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, who was it that \Nplaced you in that form?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.68,0:12:26.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What, you were lying about the traps?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.29,0:12:27.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This isn't a trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.92,0:12:42.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.82,0:12:52.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.67,0:13:00.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the one who \Ncreated these Chimera.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.73,0:13:03.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are still people here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.89,0:13:07.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you can call him a person.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.47,0:13:17.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Chimera?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.45,0:13:20.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This thing created the Chimera?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.06,0:13:24.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not all of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.72,0:13:28.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's been a long time, Edward-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.07,0:13:34.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tucker...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.44,0:13:38.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Sewing Life... Alchemist...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.93,0:13:42.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.48,0:13:44.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you here?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.56,0:13:48.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We are here because we are \Nsupposed to have been executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.84,0:13:52.72,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,It shouldn't seem strange that there would be those who are living as Chimera here too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.35,0:13:55.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not what I'm talking about!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.66,0:13:56.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.54,0:14:00.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.38,0:14:04.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That girl is dead because of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.74,0:14:07.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you still alive?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.08,0:14:09.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For Nina.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.50,0:14:13.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know well \Nhow you must feel now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.48,0:14:21.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, can't I ask you to stop going after Brother now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.13,0:14:23.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is the will of Ishbala.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.79,0:14:25.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He is an accursed alchemist—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.75,0:14:29.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and what's worse, he now \Nseeks the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.10,0:14:32.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why is alchemy so bad?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.88,0:14:35.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, your own \Nright arm has a circle,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.06,0:14:38.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,though it's one \NI've never seen before.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.48,0:14:44.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is a brand I received when I took on \Nthe calling to destroy all State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.82,0:14:48.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And as for the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.50,0:14:51.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he isn't looking for it \Nto use it in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.03,0:14:55.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's in order to return \Nmy body to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.93,0:15:00.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't know the terror \Nof the Philosopher's Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.04,0:15:01.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We do!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.52,0:15:05.30,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,There's a legend that destruction befalls those who seek the Philosopher's Stone, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.30,0:15:08.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if we were afraid of that, \Nwe'd never get our hands on anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.32,0:15:11.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come to mention it, I heard that Ishbal also perished
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.53,0:15:14.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,because it came too close \Nto the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.21,0:15:15.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.43,0:15:18.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbal did not perish.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.78,0:15:21.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was destroyed!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.03,0:15:23.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.93,0:15:26.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Open up!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.95,0:15:28.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.80,0:15:34.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, is it true?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.97,0:15:36.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've tried alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.51,0:15:46.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I failed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.44,0:15:48.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It cannot be done this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.55,0:15:49.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.97,0:15:51.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there is still the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.47,0:15:59.56,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Brother, alchemy is a heretical practice that alters the creation that God has given us!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.77,0:16:00.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.41,0:16:03.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,our god, Ishbala...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.77,0:16:06.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,will not bring her \Nback to life for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.81,0:16:19.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.96,0:16:27.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.22,0:16:28.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They mean business...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.18,0:16:31.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, it's too dangerous here!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.04,0:16:40.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.85,0:16:43.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have finally begun to see...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.66,0:16:46.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What the Philosopher's Stone is...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.10,0:16:50.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why Ishbala has forbidden it to us...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.56,0:16:51.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.94,0:16:53.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop this already!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.40,0:16:57.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The enemy is trying to destroy us \Nwith this power of the Devil!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.75,0:16:59.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.63,0:17:02.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbal will be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.67,0:17:08.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is something that has been preordained.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.30,0:17:12.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I believed that if I could obtain the Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.01,0:17:14.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,she would come back to life
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.15,0:17:17.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and Ishbal would be saved.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.56,0:17:20.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, it is for that purpose
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.49,0:17:23.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that Ishbal must be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.07,0:17:25.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.00,0:17:29.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.25,0:17:44.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.39,0:17:51.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scar-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.60,0:17:58.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know that the Philosopher's Stone \Ncan be made from people's bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.92,0:18:01.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We came to verify that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.94,0:18:04.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that's true, then we...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.76,0:18:06.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, my...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.38,0:18:11.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There sure are \Na lot of intruders today.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.09,0:18:13.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.94,0:18:14.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.37,0:18:17.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you making that face?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.94,0:18:20.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.95,0:18:22.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did he succeed?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.93,0:18:24.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.32,0:18:25.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can I eat them?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.07,0:18:30.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The armored one would be bad for your stomach.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.15,0:18:31.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll do my best!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.15,0:18:33.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculus...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.54,0:18:38.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculus?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.77,0:18:39.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They couldn't be...!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.07,0:18:45.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So the military falsified your execution
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.88,0:18:48.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and had you create Chimeras here?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.85,0:18:51.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not just Chimeras...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.24,0:18:55.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm doing research on \Na number of things...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.52,0:18:58.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that cannot be made \Npublic knowledge.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.63,0:19:03.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Spirit bonding, and other tricks \Nyou can't do with ordinary alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.58,0:19:05.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You may have become a Chimera,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.43,0:19:08.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but you still have your complete memory from when you were human.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.54,0:19:11.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who has that kind of skill?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.03,0:19:15.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Doctor Marcoh? \NBasque Grand? Someone else?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.46,0:19:19.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Answer me! \NWho the hell runs this place?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.86,0:19:27.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please don't look at them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.43,0:19:30.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're quite bashful.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.26,0:19:46.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.94,0:19:51.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They still cannot keep their shape when exposed to the open air.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.90,0:19:58.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way you're able to \Nperform human transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.23,0:20:02.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You created a Chimera... \Nto look like Nina?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.19,0:20:05.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But each time, I failed,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.00,0:20:07.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and in the end, \NI wound up in this form.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.83,0:20:11.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I'm just one step away...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.62,0:20:14.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just one step away...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.66,0:20:19.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,One... step away?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.04,0:21:05.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The unfinished Philosopher's Stone material that Doctor Marcoh had...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.10,0:21:10.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must already know that \Nit alone has considerable power.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.13,0:21:21.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If this large amount of unfinished material could be completely refined,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.93,0:21:23.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you would have a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.55,0:21:36.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Too slow!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.67,0:21:46.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, no one \Nhas yet been successful.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.84,0:21:49.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is impossible...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.22,0:21:51.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,for any ordinary alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.96,0:21:57.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.71,0:21:59.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.63,0:22:04.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,no ordinary alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.63,0:23:40.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.34,0:23:43.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 22: "Created Human"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.96,0:23:45.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculus—
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.55,0:23:48.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,a pseudo-human, \Ncreated through alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.13,0:23:53.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But they exist only in legends.
